        "title_top": "",
        "title": "Expert Backed Review Summary",
        "text": "<p>What sets the CURREX RunPro apart is its Dynamic Arch Technology™, which adapts to different arch types while allowing the foot to move naturally throughout the gait cycle. Rather than relying on stiff corrective structures, the insoles are engineered to provide flexible support that distributes pressure more evenly and helps absorb impact. Features such as a fully decoupled heel, targeted forefoot cushioning, and a zero-drop profile work together to encourage smoother transitions from heel strike to toe-off. The dual-layer cushioning system also helps manage moisture while improving underfoot comfort during longer runs. Runners often praise RunPro insoles for enhancing comfort without dramatically altering the ride of their shoes. The availability of three arch profiles allows for a more individualized fit, particularly for those who find standard sock liners lacking in support. However, it's important to recognize that these are performance insoles rather than medical orthotics. While they may help reduce stress associated with common overuse complaints and improve running comfort, they aren't intended to diagnose or treat underlying biomechanical conditions. Some users also note a slight increase in shoe weight, especially in lightweight racing models.</p>",
        "body_align": "center",
